# Test: SSH CLI exit code reflects the dispatched Response's Status field,
# not just whether d.Dispatch() itself returned a Go error.
#
# Regression target: cmd/ze/hub/service_ssh.go's responseExecErr(), wired
# into sshWireImpl's SetExecutorFactory closure. Before the fix,
# SetExecutorFactory discarded resp.Status and only returned a Go error when
# d.Dispatch() itself errored -- which many handlers deliberately avoid,
# returning Status:StatusError with a nil Go error instead (an established,
# intentional pattern: as112's handleAS112Health, internal/plugins/as112/health.go,
# and diag's HandleTCPCheck, internal/plugins/diag/cmd/tcp_check.go, both do
# this with a //nolint:nilerr comment). So a real `ze cli -c "..."` invocation
# over SSH always exited 0 regardless of Status, silently breaking any script
# (e.g. a healthcheck probe) that relies on the process exit code. The fix
# adds responseExecErr(resp, formatted), which returns a non-nil error
# whenever resp.Status == plugin.StatusError, so internal/component/ssh/ssh.go's
# exec middleware (`result, err := executor(input); if err != nil { ...
# sess.Exit(1) }`) now maps an operational failure to a nonzero exit code.
#
# Flow:
# 1. Daemon starts with a bgp {} block present AND ssh enabled. The bgp {}
#    block is load-bearing, not just a startup nicety: per cmd/ze/hub/main.go's
#    comment at the "Start SSH server directly when config has ssh {} block
#    AND no bgp {} block" branch, SSH only routes through sshWireImpl (the
#    code under test) when bgp {} is present; without it, the no-bgp{}
#    standalone path (sshBuildStandaloneImpl) wires a different executor that
#    does not go through responseExecErr at all.
# 2. The compiled driver connects directly to the fixed fixture SSH port with
#    the configured password.
# 3. `request as112 healthcheck` queries the default target 127.0.0.1:53.
#    Nothing binds the privileged port 53 in this unprivileged sandbox (see
#    test/plugin/as112-health.ci's identical rationale), so the health check
#    fails and handleAS112Health returns Status:StatusError with a nil Go
#    error. The SSH command MUST fail -- the core regression proof.
# 4. `show version` returns Status:StatusDone under normal conditions. The SSH
#    command succeeds, proving the fix did not break the success path.
#
# VALIDATES: cmd/ze/hub/service_ssh.go's responseExecErr -- the SSH exec
# session's exit code matches the dispatched Response's Status.
# PREVENTS: `ze cli -c "..."` over SSH always exiting 0 regardless of the
# command's actual outcome.

tmpfs=ssh-cli-status-error.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote { ip 127.0.0.1 }
			local { ip 127.0.0.1; accept false }
		}
		session { asn { local 65533; remote 65533 } }
	}
}

service {
	as112 { enabled true }
}

system {
	authentication {
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}

environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT2;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze start ssh-cli-status-error.conf:timeout=15s
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/ssh-cli-status-error-exit-code $PORT2:timeout=15s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: 'request as112 healthcheck' exited non-zero
expect=stderr:contains=OK: 'show version' exited 0
